// rights Unit 0 (2026-08-29) — the typecheck gate for R0.5's two CI gate files.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS. `tsconfig.json` excludes `src/**/*.test.ts`, so NOTHING
// typechecks the runtime's test files — and bun strips types at runtime, so an
// import-signature drift (say `rtPlainOwnDataForPersistence` changing shape)
// can silently weaken a gate file's assertions without any runtime error. R0.5
// hand-checked both files exit-0 through a throwaway config; that is not a gate.
//
// SCOPE IS DELIBERATELY NARROW. `evaluator.test.ts` is explicitly NOT here:
// it has never been typechecked and the cleanup is unbounded. Widening this to
// `src/**/*.test.ts` is a separate, measured decision — do not do it casually.
//
// ⚠ rights R3a ADDED ITS OWN RUNTIME SUITE, and the reason is measured rather
// than tidy. `removeInstance` gained a REQUIRED third parameter (the owner);
// `rights-r2b-partition.test.ts` called it with two, which typechecked NOWHERE
// and therefore failed only when the suite RAN — against a fixture cleanup,
// which is the quietest possible place for a gate file to break.
//
// ⚠ AND `rights-r2b-partition.test.ts` IS STILL NOT HERE, deliberately and with
// the reason named: it carries ~20 PRE-EXISTING type errors (unused imports,
// implicit `any` indexing, a duplicated object key) that predate R3a, so adding
// it would turn this gate red on work that is not R3a's. It is the largest
// remaining instance of the trap this header describes, and it is recorded in
// `workstreams/rights/notes/2026-09-13-r3a-account-owned-dispatch.md` rather
// than silently widened past.
//
// Invoked by the `r0-regression-pins` job in `.github/workflows/audit.yml`. A
// config no CI step runs closes nothing.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "src/fenel-imports.d.ts",
    "src/execute-registry-boot.test.ts",
    "src/persistence-marshalling-contract.test.ts",
    "src/rights-r3a-dispatch-ownership.test.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": []
}
